  15. A test fails when a request places content unique to it ahead of content it shares with another request of the same run.
       requirements: completion-02
       code evidence: not required — The requirement itself demands a test failure condition, so the test is the required evidence.
       test evidence: unsupported  [tier: static]
         (no mapped test)
         recommended test: A test case shows a request with unique content ordered before shared content and the test fails.
           inputs:  Construct at least two real pipeline requests from the same review run where one request contains a block shared with another request plus a later block unique to that request. Use a fixture/task that produces multiple stages or batched calls so the shared block is present in more than one request. The defective case should place the unique block before the shared block in one request.
           detects: A stage assembles its request with stage-specific or batch-specific content before the shared opening, so the reusable prefix is shortened or lost.
           full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion test-request-unique-content-after-shared-content

